+# TRACK B — Money plane (new Paystack account, webhook, payments, cutover) — PROMPT
+
+You are **Track B** of three AIs building the MyChama⇄PAY connector in parallel (A = data plane, C = experience). A foundation patch **P0** fixed all shared contracts; your patch must drop in next to theirs without conflicts.
+
+## Repos & base
+**PAY** at `6547b3a` + **P0 applied** (TypeScript, Firebase Functions v2, `africa-south1`). **Chama** at `1c83e40` (Python, project `mychama1`) — read-only for you unless a change is unavoidable. **CYBER** (WhatsApp bot) is NOT provided.
+**Read first:** `docs/mychama/CONNECTOR_CONTRACT.md`, `functions/src/mychama/contract.ts`. Frozen: `contract.ts`, `config.ts`, `errors.ts`, `sms.ts`, `paths.ts` (§10 of the contract for change requests).
+
+## Deliverables
+1. `track-B-pay-money-plane.patch` (PAY) — touching ONLY `functions/src/mychama/pay/**`, `functions/src/mychama/webhook/**` (including `handlers.ts`, which P0 moved verbatim out of `index.ts` — you own it now; keep exported signatures), `scripts/mychama/**`, `docs/mychama/cutover.md`, `docs/mychama/cyber-key-swap.md`.
+2. Optional `track-B-chama.patch` only if you find the Chama app still needs a change for the new key (it already reads `MYCHAMA_PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY` — verify by reading `functions/shared/secrets.py`, `shared/paystack.py`, `mychama/payments.py`, billing/SMS/report purchase code). Prefer config-only (document it).
+
+## B1. New webhook `mychamaPaystackCallback` (replace the P0 stub in `webhook/index.ts`)
+* Mirror the legacy `paystackCallback` in `functions/src/index.ts` (read it: signature check = HMAC-**SHA512** of `req.rawBody` vs `x-paystack-signature`, 400 on mismatch, 405 on non-POST) but with `MYCHAMA_PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY`, constant-time compare, and **MyChama references only** (`MCW- MCA- MCS- MCP- MCX- MCR-`; reuse the prefix→handler mapping logic). Non-MyChama references: log, return 200 (so Paystack doesn't retry), apply nothing.
+* Dispatch to the existing handlers in `handlers.ts` (`handleMyChamaPayment`, `…SmsTopup`, `…PlanBilling`, `…ReportCreditTopup`, `…ReportAlacarte`) and replicate the legacy `charge.failed` handling (mark the matching intent/top-up/billing/purchase doc `failed`).
+* **Bind `...MYCHAMA_HP_SECRETS`** in `secrets` (the legacy webhook does not, so the confirmation SMS has likely been failing silently — fix it here and mention it in your notes; do not edit legacy code).
+* Hardening you own in `handlers.ts`: before applying, verify Paystack `data.currency === "KES"` and that `data.amount/100` matches the stored expectation (`intent.grossAmount` for MCA/MCW; the corresponding amount field for MCS/MCP/MCX/MCR — read the Chama code that creates those docs). On mismatch: do NOT apply, set an `applyNote`, log, return 200 (permanent error ≠ retry). Transient errors → 500 so Paystack retries. Keep idempotency (`status==="success"` ⇒ no-op) and the existing spill-forward behaviour untouched.
+* Do not modify the legacy `paystackCallback` or `index.ts` — it keeps handling MyChama references until cutover (old-account in-flight payments).
+
+## B2. `mychamaPayInitiate` (replace the P0 stub in `pay/index.ts`)
+Self-pay for an authenticated PAY user who is linked to a chama (links are written by Track A under `chamaLinks/{uid}/links/*` in the plot DB — read them; only `state:"active"` links may pay; map `chamaId → memberId` from the link, **never from the client**).
+* Validate against mychama1 (read via `mychamaDb()`): chama exists/active, plan allows online collection (`PLANS[plan].onlineCollection`), `settlementSplitCode` set (else `online_collection_disabled`), member active, amount > 0 and sane, and purpose targets (`contributionId` / `loanId`+`installmentNo` / `potId`+`potPeriod` / `arrearId`) belong to that member and are payable.
+* Rate limit: mirror `MAX_INTENTS_PER_HOUR = 10` per member over `paymentIntents`; idempotency on `clientRequestId` using the **same mechanism/collection as Chama `shared/idempotency.py`** so a retry from any surface dedupes (read it carefully).
+* Fees: port Chama `functions/shared/money.py` (and check it against `Chama/src/lib/money.ts`) — `PAYSTACK_FEE_RATE 0.015`, `PAYSTACK_FEE_CAP 3000`, `CONTRIBUTION_MARKUP_RATE 0.005`, loan markup per plan, MGR = contribution markup. Put the port in `pay/fees.ts` as pure functions with test vectors in your notes (compare against several Python outputs).
+* Create the intent doc **exactly** like Chama `mychama/payments.py::initiatePayment` (field-for-field; `reference = MCA-{chamaId}-{CNT|LNR|MGR}-{epochMs}-{rand6}`; `channel:"app"`; extras `via:"pay_portal"`, `initiatedBy:{uid, role}`; `expiresAt = +30 min`), then charge mobile money via Paystack `/charge` with **`MYCHAMA_PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY`** (port `shared/paystack.py::charge_mobile_money`; metadata `chargeType:"mychama_payment"`, `targetProject:"mychama1"`, `chamaId`, `memberId`, `purpose`, `splitCode`). On Paystack failure mark the intent `failed` and throw `upstream_failure`. Default phone = member's phone on file; an explicit valid KE `phone` is allowed and recorded as `phoneOverridden`.
+* Return `PayInitiateResponse` (reference, grossAmount, paystackFee, ourFee, Paystack `display_text` as `message`).
+
+## B3. Split/subaccount migration (`scripts/mychama/`)
+Existing chamas' `settlementSplitCode`s belong to the OLD Paystack account. Investigate how settlement accounts are created in Chama (`mychama/settlement*`, `shared/paystack.py::create_split`/subaccount code, `settlementAccountRequests`) and what bank details are persisted in Firestore. If enough data is stored: write an idempotent script with `--dry-run` / `--apply`, using the NEW key, that recreates subaccount+split per chama, keeps the old code in `legacySettlementSplitCode`, writes the new `settlementSplitCode`, and reports per-chama results. If bank details are NOT stored (only inside Paystack), say so clearly and design the re-onboarding path instead (chairs re-submit settlement details; `initiatePayment` and `mychamaPayInitiate` must refuse until a new-account split exists). Note the user's finding that Paystack doesn't support their dynamic split logic, so amounts are computed in code before reaching the subaccount — keep that unchanged.
+
+## B4. Docs
+`docs/mychama/cutover.md`: ordered runbook (secrets, deploy order, test-key rehearsal, registering the new webhook URL in the new account's dashboard, split migration, switching mychama1 + CYBER to the new key, smoke tests, in-flight handling, rollback, and the exact legacy MyChama branches to delete afterwards — as a description, not applied). `docs/mychama/cyber-key-swap.md`: what to change in the CYBER repo (its MyChama flow: `MCW-` intents + charge; keep `CYBER_` flows on the old key; new secret name; split codes must exist first).
+
+## Hard rules
+* Off-limits: `contract.ts`, `config.ts`, `errors.ts`, `sms.ts`, `paths.ts`, `link/**`, `sync/**`, `index.ts`, all frontend/auth.
+* No logging of secrets/phones/ID numbers. No new npm deps unless unavoidable (list them).
+* No payment for another member, no client-supplied memberId, no trust of client-supplied fees.
+## Acceptance
+`cd functions && npx tsc --noEmit` · `npm run check:mychama-contract` · `git apply --check` (P0-only tree, and with A and C applied) · local signature test (valid/invalid/replayed event) · fee test vectors match the Python engine · emulator run of an MCA intent through to handler application.
